   "t": 26.555,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "predict",
   "t": 26.555,
   "question": "When T rises to 2, does cat stay the most likely token?",
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 26.555,
   "duration": 5.257,
   "text": "Pause here and predict. When T rises to 2, does cat stay the most likely token?",
   "bookmarks": {},
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 31.805,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 34.805,
   "duration": 7.079,
   "text": "Now raise the temperature. At T equal to two, the logits move together. The probabilities become more equal.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "hot": 36.562
   },
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 36.555,
   "mark": "hot",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 41.884,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 41.884,
   "duration": 12.549,
   "text": "Why does this happen? The ratio of two probabilities depends only on the distance between their dots. A larger distance gives a larger ratio. A smaller distance gives a ratio closer to one.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "gap": 43.443,
    "move": 48.411
   },
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 43.443,
   "mark": "gap",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 48.41,
   "mark": "move",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 54.426,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 54.426,
   "duration": 18.155,
   "text": "Why exp, and not something simpler? Divide each logit by their sum, and owl gets minus zero point four. A probability cannot be negative. Exp makes every weight positive and keeps the order. And it turns a gap into a ratio. That is why only the distance between the dots matters.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "alt": 56.718,
    "exp": 63.9
   },
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 56.71,
   "mark": "alt",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 63.893,
   "mark": "exp",
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "claim",
   "t": 63.893,
   "id": "why-exp",
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover_end",
   "t": 72.576,
   "issues": [],
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "voiceover",
   "t": 73.076,
   "duration": 9.182,
   "text": "At a very low temperature, the top token takes almost all the probability. At a very high temperature, every token gets almost the same probability.",
   "bookmarks": {
    "uni": 77.801
   },
   "scene": "SoftmaxTemperature"
  },
  {
   "kind": "bookmark",
   "t": 77.793,
   "mark": "uni",
